---
description: Comment style for all TypeScript/TSX — WHY not WHAT, tagged comments only
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commenting rules

Comments explain **why**, never **what**. Prefer fewer, clearer comments.

## Required tags

Use exactly these prefixes (colon immediately after the tag):

- `// WHY:` — why this approach / type / fallback was chosen
- `// FLOW:` — what happens next in a pipeline or handoff
- `// SECURITY:` — security decision being enforced
- `// NOTE:` — non-obvious behavior a reader must know
- `// TODO:` — known improvement, not urgent

JSX: `{/* WHY: … */}`, `{/* NOTE: … */}`, etc.

## Do

```ts
// WHY: return 404 (not 403) so job IDs cannot be enumerated.
// SECURITY: strip scripts before Puppeteer setContent.
// NOTE: sessionStorage is tab-local — drafts do not sync across tabs.
```

## Don't

- Section banners: `// ── Helpers ──`, `// === FOO ===`
- Restating the next line: `// increment counter`, `// render button`, `// handle submit`
- Untagged essays or stale audit-doc cites (`REVIEW_FINDINGS.md`, finding IDs) unless the ID is still the only pointer to an open issue
- Commenting every function/prop when names already make intent clear
- Changing logic when only cleaning comments

## When adding new code

1. Comment only non-obvious intent, races, security, or deliberate tradeoffs.
2. Always tag with `WHY:` / `FLOW:` / `SECURITY:` / `NOTE:` / `TODO:`.
3. Keep comments short; put long rationale in `CHANGELOG.md` / `CLAUDE.md` if needed.
4. Match nearby files — do not invent a new comment dialect.
